# Default-off units for a fresh DuDuClaw OS install.
#
# This must land via mkosi.skeleton/ (copied into the OS tree BEFORE the
# package manager runs — see mkosi manual, SkeletonTrees=), not
# mkosi.extra/ (copied after). Debian's openssh-server postinst enables the
# service at install time by consulting systemd's preset chain
# (systemd-sysv-generator / `deb-systemd-helper enable`, which itself reads
# /etc/systemd/system-preset/*.preset before /usr/lib/systemd/system-preset/
# *.preset) — the preset file has to already exist at that moment for
# "disable" to win, hence skeleton (pre-install) not extra (post-install).
#
# SSH stays off by default on this appliance — openssh-server is still
# installed (Packages= in mkosi.conf) so a support session can be turned
# on later (e.g. via a future dashboard toggle) without re-flashing; it
# just doesn't start out of the box on an internet-reachable device.
#
# Not independently re-verified by an actual build this round — see
# appliance/README.md "known open points" (skeleton-before-package-manager
# ordering is documented mkosi behavior, but the resulting preset outcome
# on a real Debian openssh-server postinst wasn't observed).
disable ssh.service
